From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:00:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/56] Show whitespace and line endings, and convert line
 endings

Like Notepad++ "Show symbol". View, Show whitespace draws a faint dot on
each space and an arrow across each tab; trailing whitespace is a little
stronger. View, Show line endings draws a faint mark after each line
end: the return arrow for LF, a pilcrow for CRLF, a left arrow for CR.
Both are off by default and kept in the config (show_whitespace,
show_line_endings). The marks are drawn from rectangles over the laid out
glyphs of the visible rows only, behind the text, so the text, layout and
cursor positions never change; with both off nothing is scanned.

View, "Line endings: LF" (CRLF, CR or Mixed) shows the file's line
endings and offers Convert to LF and Convert to CRLF as one undo step.
Save already writes each line's own ending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

